2026-07-15 14:39:26,107 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent received: The tender requires strict GDPR compliance, professional secrecy, confidentiality of client data, and data sovereignty. What security controls and measures would we implement to ensure the protection of sensitive data, and how would we demonstrate compliance with regulatory requirements such as LCB-FT and legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents?
2026-07-15 14:40:37,449 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-07-15 14:40:37,449 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To address the tender's requirements for strict GDPR compliance, professional secrecy, confidentiality of client data, and data sovereignty, our company, Faber IA, implements robust security controls and measures. 

We have achieved ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers the development, delivery, and operations of our services, ensuring a high standard of information security management. Additionally, we hold ISO 27701 certification, which extends our information security management system to include privacy information management.

For data protection, we utilize encryption in transit with TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest with AES-256. Our key management is based on EU-based infrastructure, ensuring that sensitive data is handled within the European Union. We also implement strict partitioning of client files with logical isolation per client and per mission, preventing any cross-client circulation of data.

To ensure GDPR compliance, we have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and maintain a data processing register. Our data protection agreements (DPAs) are aligned with GDPR Article 28, ensuring that all data processing activities are legally compliant.

Regarding professional secrecy and confidentiality, our experience in delivering services to clients bound by professional secrecy, including national professional orders, ensures that we understand the importance of maintaining confidentiality and secrecy.

To comply with LCB-FT (anti-money laundering) obligations, we are familiar with the framework and ensure that our solutions do not undermine a firm's reporting obligations. Our control mapping links platform features to applicable obligations, allowing us to produce corresponding audit evidence.

For legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents, our configurable retention policies align with legal archival obligations. We also maintain an audit log of all system activities, ensuring traceability and compliance with regulatory requirements.

Our hosting partner, OuraneCloud, holds the SecNumCloud qualification at the hosting layer, supporting sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU. This ensures that sensitive data is stored and processed in a secure environment that meets the highest standards of data sovereignty.

By leveraging these security controls and measures, we demonstrate our commitment to protecting sensitive data and complying with regulatory requirements such as GDPR, LCB-FT, and legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents.
